  "id": "emg",
  "term": "EMG",
  "definition": "EMG refers to electromyography signals, which measure muscle activation over time and can be analyzed for features such as amplitude, waveform shape, and overlap between muscles. In motor learning research, EMG is used to study how muscles work together, including co-contraction of opposing muscles during movement.",
